{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>This day</b> — a hint that the sun would stand for him, for the sun is called 'day.' <b>אחל</b> (I will begin) in gematria = <b>בחמה</b> (with the sun)." "<b>אחל</b> — three times. One instance here, and another <b>אחל גדלך</b> (Exodus 33:19, 'I will proclaim My greatness'), and another <b>ולא אחל את שם קדשי</b> (Ezekiel 39:7, 'I will not profane My holy name'). This is what they expounded: the sun stood for Moses just as it stood for Joshua. Whence do we know it speaks of the standing of the sun? For it is written, <b>ואת שם קדשי אודיע</b> ('I will make known My holy name'), and <b>ולא אחל את שם קדשי עוד</b> ('I will not profane My holy name anymore') — and with the standing of the sun His holy name was made known in all the earth."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:08:38.445172631Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}